  ('easing-perfectionism', 1, 'Write down one task you have been polishing for too long, and decide what "done" looks like for it in a single sentence.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 2, 'Send one email today without rereading it a second time.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 3, 'Notice the standard you are holding yourself to on one task, and ask whether anyone else expects that from you.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 4, 'Pick a small chore, set a timer for ten minutes, and stop when it rings even if it is not finished.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 5, 'Leave one typo in a text message to a friend and send it anyway.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 6, 'Choose a task you tend to over-prepare for and cut your preparation time in half today.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 7, 'Cook dinner tonight without measuring anything exactly, and eat it without commenting on what went wrong.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 8, 'Hand a task to someone else at home or at work today and let them do it their way, start to finish.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 9, 'Before starting one piece of work, write the lowest bar it needs to clear, then aim for that bar and no higher.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 10, 'Make your bed a little sloppily on purpose and leave it that way all day.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 11, 'Rate a piece of your work from one to ten, then ask what a seven would have looked like and whether it would have done the job.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 12, 'Post a photo on social media without editing it or checking how the light looks.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 13, 'Ask a coworker what they think a finished version of a shared task looks like, and notice if their bar is lower than yours.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 14, 'Notice one thing you avoided starting today because you could not do it well, and spend five minutes doing it badly.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 15, 'Wear the outfit you put together first this morning, without changing any part of it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 16, 'Say "that is good enough" out loud at the end of one task today, and mean it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 17, 'Send a draft to someone before you think it is ready and ask for their reaction.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 18, 'Hang a picture or shelf in your home without measuring, then decide whether anyone would ever notice.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 19, 'Make a list of everything you did today, then circle the items where extra effort would have changed nothing.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 20, 'Let your child, partner, or roommate load the dishwasher their way and do not rearrange it afterward.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 21, 'Write a rough first draft of something in fifteen minutes with your spell-checker turned off.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 22, 'Pick one recurring task and decide, in writing, how much time it deserves from now on.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 23, 'Serve guests or family a meal on mismatched plates and notice whether anyone cares.'),
