  ('easing-perfectionism', 280, 'Adjust an appointment, a plan, or a route on the fly instead of starting over from a clean plan.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 281, 'Take a walk without a destination, a step goal, or a podcast.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 282, 'Keep a running list this week of mistakes that turned out not to matter, and add one today.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 283, 'Trust a store clerk, a mechanic, or a neighbor''s recommendation instead of researching it yourself.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 284, 'Turn the sound off on the parts of a task you cannot control, such as how it will be received, and finish the part you can.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 285, 'Give a rough answer to "how long will this take?" and let the estimate be wrong.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 286, 'Move a project from your "someday, when I am ready" list to "start with what I have," and spend twenty minutes on it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 287, 'Spend a rainy afternoon making something with no plan for how it should turn out.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 288, 'Release a small piece of work to a wider audience than you normally would.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 289, 'Refuse to redo one thing today that already works.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 290, 'Set a "no restarting" rule for the next creative session and keep going even when the beginning is weak.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 291, 'Cut the number of items in a presentation, plan, or email in half and send the shorter one.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 292, 'Sit through a meal you cooked without listing what you would do differently next time.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 293, 'Deal with an error you find in old work by asking whether anyone was harmed, and if not, leave it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 294, 'Start the day by naming one thing you will let be imperfect, and check in at bedtime to see whether it mattered.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 295, 'Introduce yourself to someone new without steering the conversation to show your best side.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 296, 'Trim a hedge, a beard, or a fringe of hair in one careful pass, then step back rather than evening it out endlessly.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 297, 'Look at an inbox with ten replies waiting and answer all ten in twenty minutes, plainly.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 298, 'Bring a friend into a task you usually do alone because only you do it right, and share the work.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 299, 'Complete an online course lesson without taking notes on every detail.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 300, 'Allow one visible imperfection in your holiday table, such as a paper napkin or a store-bought pie.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 301, 'Speak a few sentences in a language you are learning to someone who speaks it, expecting to get some of it wrong.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 302, 'Give your best guess on a quiz, form, or trivia question instead of looking it up.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 303, 'Photograph your meal, your project, or your view once and put the camera down.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 304, 'Pass your notes to a colleague in their raw state, without tidying them first.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 305, 'Trust yourself to remember a short list instead of writing it down and checking it twice.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 306, 'Leave a comment on a friend''s post with a single emoji or a single word.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 307, 'Write your holiday or vacation plans on one page and stop planning there.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 308, 'Skip the practice run for a small recipe, speech, or route and do the real thing first.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 309, 'Allow a sibling, parent, or partner to wrap the gifts their way.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 310, 'Dress for comfort at a family event and notice how much attention your clothes actually receive.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 311, 'Redefine a "bad" workout as one you did not do, and count everything else as good.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 312, 'Say "I do not know yet" to a question at work and let the sentence sit without filling the silence.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 313, 'Leave the last dish in the sink overnight.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 314, 'Tell a story at dinner without worrying about getting every detail right.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 315, 'Frame a piece of your own art or your child''s, flaws included, and hang it in a room you use every day.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 316, 'Aim to be on time rather than early for one appointment, and see whether anything changes.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 317, 'Pick the first name that comes to mind for a document, folder, project, or pet, and keep it.'),
