  ('easing-perfectionism', 327, 'Hand in a form, essay, or report with an answer you are only fairly sure about.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 328, 'Go to bed with a small mess in the kitchen and see how you feel about it in the morning.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 329, 'Say something in a meeting that is useful but not brilliant.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 330, 'Cook without tasting and adjusting the seasoning more than once.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 331, 'Ask a colleague to take a task off your plate that only you have ever done, and walk them through it once, not three times.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 332, 'Write a limerick, a joke, or a caption that is only mildly funny, and share it anyway.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 333, 'Pull one thing from your "redo" pile and decide to leave it exactly as it is, permanently.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 334, 'Skip color-coding, labeling, or sorting for a project this week, and notice whether the work still gets done.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 335, 'Send a rough sketch or wireframe to a client or teammate instead of a finished mockup.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 336, 'Buy the paint, the plant, or the frame that is in stock rather than ordering the exact one you pictured.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 337, 'Practice handing something over with the words "here is a start" instead of "sorry, it is not finished."'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 338, 'Delegate the family''s dinner plans to the person least likely to plan them your way.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 339, 'Walk out the door with a coat that does not match your shoes.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 340, 'Name the standard you set for a task this morning, then set it one notch lower before you begin.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 341, 'Give a toast, a thank-you, or a welcome from the heart without notes or a rehearsal.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 342, 'Take a beginner''s swimming, dance, or pottery class and enjoy being the worst in the room for an hour.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 343, 'Leave a piece of furniture assembled with one small part done imperfectly, as long as it is safe and stable.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 344, 'Answer a survey, a quiz, or a form quickly instead of weighing each option.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 345, 'Stop editing a photo or a video after the second change.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 346, 'Bake bread or cookies and let them be a little misshapen, then share them the same day.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 347, 'Ask a teammate to send you their "rough enough" version of something, and thank them for not polishing it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 348, 'Let one of your children or a younger relative teach you something, and let yourself do it wrong the first few times.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 349, 'Spend twenty minutes on a task you would normally give two hours, and see how much of the result you keep.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 350, 'Look for one place in your day where perfect and good would look identical to everyone else, and choose good.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 351, 'Turn off the "one more pass" instinct on a chore tonight by setting a timer for five minutes and quitting at the bell.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 352, 'Deliver a piece of work early and rough rather than late and polished.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 353, 'Wash your hair, skip the styling, and go about your day.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 354, 'Set a limit of three drafts for anything you write this week, and hit send on the third.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 355, 'Give a piece of feedback to someone without softening it into perfection or over-explaining.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 356, 'Assemble a meal from leftovers without a recipe and serve it with a name you make up on the spot.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 357, 'Choose a workout on the spot from whatever equipment or space is in front of you rather than the ideal plan.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 358, 'Take a family photo where someone is blinking, and keep it as the official one.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 359, 'Read an instruction manual once and then try the device, expecting to figure out the rest by using it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 360, 'Let the guest room have a few of your things in it when someone stays over.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 361, 'Trust your first ranking of options today, whether jobs, restaurants, or paint chips, and act on it.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 362, 'Notice how much you enjoy a task once you stop grading it, and stay in that mode for the rest of the hour.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 363, 'Finish today''s version of a long project, save it, and close the file without opening it again tonight.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 364, 'Practice letting a small error stand in a conversation: do not correct the date, name, or detail you got slightly wrong.'),
  ('easing-perfectionism', 365, 'End the day by naming one imperfect thing you finished, and let that be what you remember about today.')
